  "question": {
    "html": "<p>When the potential difference between two parallel metal plates is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"V\"></span> and the distance between the plates is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"D\"></span>, the electric field strength between the plates is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E\"></span>.</p>\n<p>What is the new electric field strength between the plates when the potential difference is halved and the distance is doubled?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{E}{2}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{E}{4}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{E}{8}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
